TUnit uses `[Before(...)]` and `[After(...)]` attributes with a hook type to control scope. Here's a sketch for each:

## 1. Before/After Every Test (method-level)

```csharp
public class MyTests
{
    [Before(Test)]
    public void ResetDatabase(TestContext context)
    {
        // runs before each [Test] in this class
    }

    [After(Test)]
    public void Cleanup(TestContext context) { }

    [Test]
    public async Task SomeTest() { /* ... */ }
}
```

## 2. Once Per Class (class-level)

```csharp
public class MyTests
{
    [Before(Class)]
    public static void OpenFixture(ClassHookContext context)
    {
        // runs once before the first test in this class
    }

    [After(Class)]
    public static void DisposeFixture(ClassHookContext context)
    {
        // runs once after the last test in this class
    }

    [Test]
    public async Task Test1() { /* ... */ }
}
```

> Class-level hooks must be **static**.

## 3. Once Per Assembly

```csharp
public class GlobalSetup
{
    [Before(Assembly)]
    public static void StartWireMock(AssemblyHookContext context)
    {
        // runs once before any test in this assembly
    }

    [After(Assembly)]
    public static void StopWireMock(AssemblyHookContext context)
    {
        // runs once after all tests in this assembly
    }
}
```

The class doesn't need any special base class — TUnit discovers these hooks by attribute.

## 4. Once Per Entire Test Session

```csharp
public class SessionLifecycle
{
    [Before(TestSession)]
    public static void ApplyMigrations(TestSessionContext context)
    {
        // very first thing to run across all assemblies
    }

    [After(TestSession)]
    public static void TearDownDatabase(TestSessionContext context)
    {
        // very last thing to run
    }
}
```

---

### Summary Table

| Scope | Attribute | Method must be | Context parameter |
|-------|-----------|---------------|-------------------|
| Each test | `[Before(Test)]` / `[After(Test)]` | Instance | `TestContext` |
| Class | `[Before(Class)]` / `[After(Class)]` | **static** | `ClassHookContext` |
| Assembly | `[Before(Assembly)]` / `[After(Assembly)]` | **static** | `AssemblyHookContext` |
| Session | `[Before(TestSession)]` / `[After(TestSession)]` | **static** | `TestSessionContext` |

All hooks can be `async Task` if needed. The enum values (`Test`, `Class`, `Assembly`, `TestSession`) come from `TUnit.Core.HookType`.
